Package: cqrfdr
Type: Package
Title: FDR-Controlled Variable Selection for High-Dimensional Censored Quantile Regression
Version: 0.3.0
Date: 2026-10-22
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jinzhao", "Yu", role = "aut"),
    person("Zili", "Liu", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "ZLiu20@mdanderson.org"))
Description: Variable selection with false discovery rate control for
    high-dimensional censored quantile regression. The single-split
    mirror-statistic procedure (SS-MS) fits the sequential L1-penalized
    Peng-Huang estimator of Zheng, Peng and He (2018, Annals of Statistics)
    on one half of the data, refits the screened model without penalty on the
    other half, and selects covariates by a data-driven threshold on mirror
    statistics. Its multiple-splitting version (MS-MS) aggregates SS-MS over
    many random splits through inclusion rates for a more stable selection.
    The package also provides the single and multiple data splitting procedures
    of Dai, Lin, Xing and Liu (2023, Journal of the American Statistical
    Association), the penalized sequential estimator with cross-validated,
    pivotal or Zheng-Peng-He penalties, and a simulator for the designs used in
    the accompanying paper.
